WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.080
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Monday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.430
Here's what happened in transhumanism in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.540
Show your work. A startup's AI just solved an 18-year-old quantum puzzle,

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.600
and software checked every step.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.020
An audit says Anthropic's AI improves twice as fast.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.390
The evidence? Mostly redacted.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.710
OpenAI says its new model found 81 serious Firefox bugs,

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.310
and Mozilla's already shipping fixes.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.130
DeepMind's agents found two weak spots in old,

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.640
retired encryption. Today's longer keys are safe.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.560
OpenAI also tested AI on 100 everyday lab tasks.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.580
Its best model scored about two-thirds.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.850
In a Toronto preprint, AI agents rehearse experiments in a virtual lab,

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.630
then run the real robots.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.040
In an early trial,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.760
off-the-shelf gene-edited immune cells helped all nine patients with an autoimmune muscle disease.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.570
In two big trials,

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:14.060
Lilly's experimental jab at least halved knee arthritis pain for about two in three people.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.190
In a tiny trial,

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:21.700
engineered clean-up cells cut serious setbacks for failing livers by 42%.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.740
In 88,000 older adults, 42 bright minutes a day went with 17% less dementia.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.100
On to wellbeing. In a trial with expectant mums,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.770
twelve short online sessions kept anxiety from climbing.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.520
In a small trial,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.490
a month of sleeping with an air filter smoothed blood sugar swings in prediabetes.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.310
Now, the catch. A drug cut a risky blood fat by 78%. Heart attacks? Unchanged.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.550
Here in Australia,

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.730
the income gap in who gets subsidised therapy nearly doubled; poorer kids miss out most.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.850
SpaceX aims to catch both halves of Starship with its tower,

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.440
as soon as November 13.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.970
And physicists made a supersolid, part crystal,

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.960
part frictionless fluid, at room temperature.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.730
And six humanoid robots ran a Shanghai shop for a whole day.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.700
Four of the six passed review.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.720
So, whether it's maths, medicine or machines,

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.650
show your work. That's how we know what's real.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.310
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.320
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
